n and those  images released to the public I'm  talking about like personal details yeah  yeah I think because those are the  victims and aren't the perpetrators I  think they have every right to have  their identity sealed  how about words with words I'm Way more  loose I mean I I think it's there are  very few situations where I would  advocate the self-censorship of words  when it comes to explaining what  happened in a news story for me it's  more about decisions on graphic videos  and pictures yeah especially with words  that the word that comes to my mind is  the n-word because if you're quoting  someone else using that in context I  think  most news reporters are weary of wording  them of quoting them verbatim yeah  that's a very tricky thing I I think  that that's interesting I mean I tend to  like I don't use the n-word personally  but I don't know that we do remoting  someone else yeah I don't even know that  we have necessarily a policy on the show  but generally speaking like if we have a  video or a quote from someone else we'll  will use the full n-word I think that's  generally the policy and again our  decisions are more based on there are  certain words which our broadcast  affiliates cannot air because they will  get fined by the FCC  we obviously censor those but beyond  that we tend not to censor yeah and then  when it comes to images and video clips  we also yeah we have this debate every  time one comes up because there was an  assassination of one of those Russian  official yeah a few weeks ago right and  we had this we really just opened it up  to the audience over whether or not we  should show it show the video yeah yeah  um one other thought on this there are  some people who will hear me saying  David oh my god Davey you're such a  special snowflake trigger warnings safe  space clown [ __ ] or whatever right the  truth is that this isn't about being a  special snowflake or being triggered or  whatever it's about do we need to show  anything that we can find simply for the  sake of being salacious and inflammatory  and if it leads it bleeds type of thing  and so for me the question is not am I  trying to protect people it's a my  crafting a story that is fully  informative and do I need to go out of  my way to include graphic images if they  don't actually add to the telling of the  story that's my standard I agree with  that policy yeah you shouldn't go out of  your way to include information that's  not necessary or pertinent to the story  but if everyone else is reporting in the  same way I think you should go along  with that
 

